  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fix The Loan Msmes, Farmers &amp;Taxpayers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FIX THE LOAN FOR MSMES, FARMERS AND TAXPAYERS: The Uganda Ministry of Agriculture&apos;s (MAAIF) proposal for how to spend a 350 millionEuro loan from the UK Export Financing Facility targeted to export infrastructure (facilities and equipment), has ignored all inputwhich micro, small and medium agriculture enterprises (MSMEs),including those representing farmers, have suggested to make the loanrelevant to the needs of the farmers and agricultural MSMEs. Membership associations representing these agricultural MSMEs and farmers will join with Uganda Agribusiness Alliance in providing information to and organizing an advocacy action plan with a wider selection of private sector organizations in order to advocate for cutting out wasteful parts of the proposal, making other parts of theproposed project public-private partnershipsimplemented by agriculture associations, cooperatives or MSMEs, and other parts available to agriculture associations, cooperatives or MSMEs on a lease-with-option-to-buy basis that will both provide lease revenue to help pay of the loan, as well as result in these private sector bodies acquiring an asset that can help them increase their ability toget financing in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
