  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda Agribusiness Alliance  (UAA) was founded in 2014 in order to to help catalyze sustainable investment and growth in Ugandan agribusiness by contributing to better policy-making, informing business decisions, sharing best practices, facilitating collaboration and engaging stakeholders beyond commercial objectives. Founders were domestic stakeholders drawn from the private sector, holdingbackgrounds and qualifications including: law, finance, government, economics, public service, academia, agriculture and entrepreneurship.

Under the Fair 4 All program, Uganda Agribusiness Alliance (UAA) will be reponsible for ensuring that participation of smallholder farmers are  considered in all engagements and facilitated and/or supported.  Uganda Agribusiness Alliance,  already convenemajor stakeholders of some of the horticultural value chain crops in major platforms and therefore,  Fair4All program will leverageon this connections to ensure that the benefits that accrues from regional and global horticultural crop value chains trickle to smallholder food producers in more equal proportions. This they will do by creating platforms for building healthy commercial relationships among smallholder farmers, exporters, local traders and policy makers.

Uganda Agribusiness Alliance will also build capacity of exporters and horticulture farmers to ensure they meet the markets standards that will facilitate their full realization of gainsfrom the horticulture value chains.  UAA is also expected to connect withOxfam and other Fair4All implementing partner organizations to inform them on key areas of engagements with smallholder farmers to ensure they tap optimal benefits from horticulture value chains.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda Agribusiness Alliance</narrative>
  </participating-org>
